1 Download the iso https://www.debian.org/releases/bookworm/debian-installer/
2 Flash the usb stick or cd
3 Setup Debian 12
4 When on Software Selection Deselect GNOME and debian desktop environment leaving it empty
5 After install login as root first
6 Run apt install links
7 Run links https://github.com/syslacklinux/Forsaken-Linux then find Screenshot From 2026-07-1713-56-15 then save then change then name from 623065669-de80debd-40f3-4822-8c91-d3403ed04c46 to forsaken-logo.png then exit links
8 run ls /root
9 run mv /root/forsaken-logo.png /usr/share/pixmaps
  Then run cp /usr/share/pixmaps/forsaken-logo.png /usr/share/pixmaps/debian-logo.png
10 Run nano /etc/os-release
   Change

PRETTY_NAME="Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm)"
NAME="Debian GNU/Linux"
VERSION_ID="12"
VERSION="12 (bookworm)"
VERSION_CODENAME=bookworm
ID=debian
HOME_URL="https://www.debian.org/"
SUPPORT_URL="https://www.debian.org/support"
BUG_REPORT_URL="https://bugs.debian.org/"

TO

PRETTY_NAME="Forsaken Linux 2 (stalemate)"
NAME="Forsaken Linux"
VERSION_ID="2"
VERSION="2 (stalemate)"
VERSION_CODENAME=stalemate
ID=forsaken
HOME_URL="https://github.com/syslacklinux/Forsaken-Linux"
SUPPORT_URL="https://github.com/syslacklinux/Forsaken-Linux/discussions/1"
BUG_REPORT_URL="https://github.com/syslacklinux/Forsaken-Linux/issues"
LOGO=/usr/share/pixmaps/forsaken-logo.png

CTRL X Y ENTER and prevent from getting resetted by running apt-mark hold base-files

11 Run nano /etc/issue then change Debian GNU/Linux 12 \n \l to Welcome to \s \r \m (\l)
12 Run rm /etc/issue.net
13 Run nano /etc/default/grub
   Then change GRUB_DISTRIBUTOR='lsb_release -i -s 2> /dev/null || echo Debian' to GRUB_DISTRIBUTOR="Forsaken"
   On GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT Remove quiet so it will be GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT=""
CTRL X Y Enter then update-grub

14 Run apt install bsdgames fortune
15 run rm /etc/motd
16 Create a Forsaken origin file nano /etc/dpkg/origins/forsaken
   Add 
Vendor: Forsaken Linux
Vendor-URL: https://github.com/syslacklinux/Forsaken-Linux
Bugs: https://github.com/syslacklinux/Forsaken-Linux/issues

CTRL X Y ENTER Then ln -sf /etc/dpkg/origins/forsaken /etc/dpkg/origins/default
17 run apt install sudo then nano /etc/sudoers
   then add your username on User privilege specification
   then after root ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL add username ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL (Change username to your username)
CTRL X Y Enter
18 Run apt update then apt full-upgrade
